<title>HUNGARY: Hungarian Parliament approves 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Hungarian Parliament approves 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Parliament on Tuesday approved the country's 1997 central state budget law.</p>
<p>The law targets a central state budget deficit of 309 billion forints for 1997, compared with the 302 billion forints originally proposed by the government when debate began two months ago, and a forecast deficit of 150 to 170 billion forints for 1996.</p>
<p>The one-chamber Parliament, where the ruling Socialist-Liberal coalition holds 278 of the 386 seats, approved the 1997 budget law with 257 votes in favour, 80 against and two abstentions.</p>
</text>
